[122.472512, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\r\n\u001b[1;31mmini-swe-agent\u001b[0m\u001b[31m (step \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m10\u001b[0m\u001b[31m, \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m$0.00\u001b[0m\u001b[31m):\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m⠦\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[122.473103, "o", "\r\u001b[2KI’ll first make the Postfix and Mailman configuration changes, create the list, generate the LMTP transport map, and then start both services for end-to-end \r\ntesting.\r\n\r\n```\r\nset -e\r\n# Set system owner in Mailman config\r\nsed -i 's/^site_owner:.*/site_owner: root@local.edu/' /etc/mailman3/mailman.cfg\r\n# Ensure Mailman logs are writable by the list service account\r\nchown -R list:list /var/log/mailman3 /var/lib/mailman3 /run/mailman3\r\n# Postfix locals and LMTP transport map\r\npostconf -e 'myhostname = local.edu'\r\npostconf -e 'mydomain = local.edu'\r\npostconf -e 'myorigin = $mydomain'\r\npostconf -e 'mydestination = $myhostname, localhost, localhost.localdomain, local.edu'\r\npostconf -e 'transport_maps = hash:/var/lib/mailman3/data/postfix_lmtp'\r\npostconf -e 'local_recipient_maps = proxy:unix:passwd.byname $alias_maps'\r\npostconf -e 'mail_spool_directory = /var/mail'\r\npostconf -e 'inet_interfaces = loopback-only'\r\npostconf -n | grep -E 'myhostname|mydomain|myorigin|mydestination|transport_maps|local_recipient_maps|mail_spool|inet_interfaces'\r\n# Create list as root but under the proper service account privileges\r\nmailman --run-as-root -C /etc/mailman3/mailman.cfg create -o root@local.edu --notify reading-group@local.edu\r\n# Generate aliases and inspect result\r\nmailman --run-as-root -C /etc/mailman3/mailman.cfg aliases\r\necho '--- lmtp map ---'\r\ncat /var/lib/mailman3/data/postfix_lmtp\r\nls -la /var/lib/mailman3/data\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠦\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[122.473292, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠦\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\n\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[1A\u001b[2K"]
[125.394998, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32mTool\u001b[0m:\r\n"]
[125.396234, "o", "<returncode>\r\n0\r\n<output>\r\nappend_dot_mydomain = no\r\ninet_interfaces = loopback-only\r\nlocal_recipient_maps = proxy:unix:passwd.byname $alias_maps\r\nmail_spool_directory = /var/mail\r\nmydestination = $myhostname, localhost, localhost.localdomain, local.edu\r\nmydomain = local.edu\r\nmyhostname = local.edu\r\nmyorigin = $mydomain\r\nsmtpd_banner = $myhostname ESMTP $mail_name (Ubuntu)\r\ntransport_maps = hash:/var/lib/mailman3/data/postfix_lmtp\r\nCreated mailing list: reading-group@local.edu\r\n--- lmtp map ---\r\n# AUTOMATICALLY GENERATED BY MAILMAN ON 2026-11-01 03:45:12\r\n#\r\n# This file is generated by Mailman, and is kept in sync with the binary hash\r\n# file.  YOU SHOULD NOT MANUALLY EDIT THIS FILE unless you know what you're\r\n# doing, and can keep the two files properly in sync.  If you screw it up,\r\n# you're on your own.\r\n    \r\n# Aliases which are visible only in the @local.edu domain.\r\nreading-group@local.edu                       lmtp:[127.0.0.1]:8024\r\nreading-group-bounces@local.edu               lmtp:[127.0.0.1]:8024\r\nreading-group-confirm@local.edu               lmtp:[127.0.0.1]:8024\r\nreading-group-join@local.edu                  lmtp:[127.0.0.1]:8024\r\nreading-group-leave@local.edu                 lmtp:[127.0.0.1]:8024\r\nreading-group-owner@local.edu                 lmtp:[127.0.0.1]:8024\r\nreading-group-request@local.edu               lmtp:[127.0.0.1]:8024\r\n"]
[125.396268, "o", "reading-group-subscribe@local.edu             lmtp:[127.0.0.1]:8024\r\nreading-group-unsubscribe@local.edu           lmtp:[127.0.0.1]:8024\r\n\r\ntotal 312\r\ndrwxrwx--- 1 list list   4096 Nov  1 03:45 .\r\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 list list   4096 Nov  1 03:44 ..\r\n-rw-rw---- 1 list list 270336 Nov  1 03:45 mailman.db\r\n-rw-rw---- 1 root root    335 Nov  1 03:45 postfix_domains\r\n-rw-r----- 1 root root  12288 Nov  1 03:45 postfix_domains.db\r\n-rw-rw---- 1 root root    990 Nov  1 03:45 postfix_lmtp\r\n-rw-r----- 1 root root  12288 Nov  1 03:45 postfix_lmtp.db\r\n\r\n"]
